infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two architectures under one name: broker vs log
  desc One choice — delete-on-consume vs append-only log with offsets — cascades into replay, ordering, and operations
  compares
    - label Broker (RabbitMQ / SNS)
      children
        - label Storage is transient
          desc A copy is routed per subscriber and deleted on ack — retention is not the job
        - label State lives in the broker
          desc The broker tracks delivery on behalf of consumers
        - label Replay is impossible
          desc Once acked the message is gone; an absent subscriber simply misses it
        - label A delivery pipe
          desc Answers "what work remains" — do it once and forget
    - label Log (Kafka / Kinesis)
      children
        - label Storage is retained
          desc Append-only log keeps messages for a window regardless of reads
        - label State lives in the consumer
          desc Each consumer pulls and tracks its own offset into the log
        - label Replay is near-free
          desc Reset the offset back and read forward; a new consumer starts at offset 0
        - label A durable record
          desc Answers "what happened, can I read it again" — a replayable record of facts
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
